ed Hand\u201d or \u201cAll Pungs\u201d-style pattern, the resulting hand structure would be five melds and no pair \u2014 which violates the fundamental requirement of four melds and a pair (or a recognized special hand). Without a pair, the hand cannot win. Since no winning hand can be formed by performing Peng W1, the only logical choice is to pass, avoiding an illegal play.]\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
